{
	title: 'Safe model clear and compact with attributed continuation',
	spec: 'Hal and humans can issue /compact and /clear while a turn runs. The host mechanically applies context boundaries only after active work settles and every dispatched tool call has a recorded result, never between a call and its result. /compact preserves the active turn prompts, compacts between rounds, and continues the same turn without a model-authored follow-up. /clear ends the old turn before resetting; no further old-context provider request or later tool dispatch occurs after an accepted clear. Undispatched calls receive explicit not-run results. A clear submitted while streaming cancels the request and waits for settlement; a foreground tool is allowed to settle safely. A model command must acknowledge its pending transition without awaiting its own turn. Idle operations run immediately. /clear accepts an optional prompt as the entire raw argument tail, including multiline content: no shell quote parsing, implicit file loading, or slash-command execution of the generated prompt. With a prompt it records the reset and a normal prompt and starts a fresh turn; without one it remains idle. Already-empty contexts still start a supplied prompt. Preserve cwd, model, draft, name, history and unrelated inbox messages. Pending transitions and completion are durable and deduplicated through crash recovery; a crash cannot lose an accepted continuation or inject it twice. Escape cancels pending automatic continuation and must not silently restart a paused session. Conflicting pending resets must be refused visibly rather than overwritten. No new generic scheduler or message type is required. Sender identity is inherited from the command through the mechanical generation step, not recursively through model decisions. Host-established command provenance reaches command execution context and the continuation prompt, using existing from/label and origin: model plus a generating-command field. Both live and replayed headers show You (/clear continuation), Hal (/clear continuation), or Message from <sender> (/clear continuation); cross-session command records instead show Command from <sender>. Self-issued commands retain Hal (command). The provider sees attribution too, so a model-generated prompt cannot masquerade as a human instruction. All sender propagation, prompt framing, history/protocol validation and human recall/edit ownership respect the new origin metadata. Both clients share title formatting, with no recursive ancestry tree or hard-coded attribution in prompt body. Restore the invariant that context boundaries do not split tool exchanges and live/reloaded/recovered views and sender attribution agree. Add focused behavioral tests for self-issued compact/clear, safe settlement and undispatched calls, human clear during streaming/tools, idle/empty and multiline/literal slash continuations, pause cancellation, crash recovery/deduplication, sender framing and live/replay parity. Help and model tool descriptions explain behavior.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"Intent lives on the accepting command's output record (transition); transitionCancel/transitionDone outputs settle it. Boundaries and continuation prompts carry the intent id, so recovery after any crash gap skips work already recorded and never injects twice. pages.marks and busy keep pending intents in closed tabs.",
		'Clear must record results for every unanswered call before the old turn_end, including during crash recovery; recovery used to write turn_end first. Bare clear from paused, error or a parked approval ends idle: the turn_end closes the question and held calls never resume.',
		"Compaction may summarize a first turn with no earlier prompt when it holds assistant or tool entries; the old 'nothing to summarize without a prompt' rule refused self-issued /compact in turn one. Scope unchanged otherwise.",
		"Only /clear gets the literal raw tail (one separator consumed); other commands keep whitespace-normalized args so paths and flags parse as before. Completion outputs are durable but hidden live and in replay to avoid noise after 'Context cleared.'",
		'turns.ts hit the 400-line limit: policy helpers moved to turn-policy.ts and record validation to history-check.ts instead of deleting docs. Under full-suite load turns-retry and slash timing tests flake occasionally; they pass repeatedly in isolation and at base.'
	],
	needs: ['vh', 'bc', 'rj', 'hp'],
